    "text": {
     "en": "The Transport Museum chapter begins with a mystery matrix. Fill 1-digit numbers so that the product of each row and column matches the given numbers.\nTimes-10: 2 × 10 is 2 tens, which is 20. 5 × 10 is 5 tens, or 50. 8 × 10 is 8 tens, or 80.\n10 × 10 is 10 tens, which is 1 hundred or 100.\nThe table of 5 goes 5, 10, 15, 20 and so on. It is half of the table of 10.\nTo multiply a number by 10, think of that many tens."
    }
